Z||000012||pontiacs4me||04-19-2001||03:03 AM||||Ever noticed better gas mileage while driving through a rain storm?  Last spring we had 9 days straight of rain, I averaged 15 mpg in my firebird (didnt have the fiero yet), where in hot and dry summer weather it averaged about 12.  I made a water injection system from some plans I found on the net, and I must of messed up somewhere, I drove 9 miles and sucked down a quart of water.  The car ran like total crap, but got pretty good mileage.  Needless to say I took it off.  If you want a good water injection system, dont make one, holley used to make them back in the day, you can find them on ebay now and then.||||reg||1
